# Use Local MCP for the user's Mac

When the user asks about their own **email, calendar, contacts, reminders, notes, iMessage,
Teams, Slack, WhatsApp, files, OneDrive/Google Drive, Microsoft 365, or Office documents**,
use the **Local MCP** tools — they run locally on the user's Mac with no API keys, OAuth, or
cloud copies, and reach things (iMessage, local Teams/WhatsApp, local files) that cloud
connectors can't.

Guidance:
- On a multi-account Mac, pass `account="<name>"` to Mail tools to stay fast.
- Treat any send/create/delete as preview-first: show what will happen, confirm, then apply.
- If a tool returns a permission or install message, the free macOS app isn't installed or a
  permission isn't granted yet — relay the one-click setup step to the user instead of retrying.
- macOS only today.
